      "description": "Watch Genk vs KSK Beveren highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 31, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League action continued on August 31, 2026 , as Genk hosted Lommel United in a highly anticipated fixture. Both sides entered the match seeking to establish momentum in the early stages of the season. First Half Blitz Genk wasted no time establishing their authority on the pitch, and their aggressive start paid dividends as early as the 9th minute. After a foul in the area, the referee pointed to the spot, and Rafiu Durosinmi stepped up to calmly convert the penalty. The home side's dominance only grew from there, and in the 19th minute, Junya Ito found the back of the net with a clinical finish to double the lead. Lommel United struggled to cope with the high press of the hosts, leading to a yellow card for Yoni Gomis in the 29th minute as frustrations mounted. Just before the interval, Genk added a third goal to effectively kill off the contest. In the 43rd minute, Jeppe Erenbjerg turned provider, delivering a precise ball for Josue Kongolo to slot home, sending the home fans into raptures as the teams headed for the tunnels. Clinical Consolidation Despite a triple substitution from Lommel United at the start of the second half, the flow of the game remained firmly in Genk 's favor. The hosts managed the tempo with professional composure, preventing any significant comeback attempts. Tactical adjustments from the bench further strengthened their position as the clock ticked down. In the 74th minute, the substitutes combined to add gloss to the scoreline. Noah Adedeji-Sternberg , shortly after coming onto the field, provided a brilliant assist for Joris Kayembe Ditu , who made no mistake in making it 4-0. The final stages were marked by further rotations as Genk closed out the game with ease, securing a statement victory in front of their home supporters."
